{
  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_041 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 3.60 GPU-hrs, with config_025 (concat fusion) a close second at 0.721. Multiprofile + transformer aggregation + scvi_n200 + weighted fusion is strongly supported. However, the image encoder has only been tested as imagenet_vit_l in this top-performing architecture. Question: Does swapping to resnet50 (config_015) preserve the 0.725-level accuracy, or is ViT-L's larger representational capacity critical? This is the single most unexplored axis in the best-performing setup. Rationale: With 4 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out the image encoder's contribution is high-value—if resnet50 matches, we save ~1+ GPU-hr per run and can redirect budget; if it underperforms, we lock in ViT-L and focus remaining experiments on fine-tuning. Expected relative cost: moderate, roughly 2.5–3.5 GPU-hrs (resnet50 is substantially lighter than ViT-L, reducing the dominant image-encoding cost while retaining transformer aggregation over multiprofile). This is the best use of experiment 6 because it reduces uncertainty on a major architectural choice without repeating any prior configuration."
}

